  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Max discovers Senya was poisoned by their fake cognac. Viktor asks Kostya for a bottle of cognac and accidentally takes the fake one. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, это просто ужас!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня отравился нашим коньяком.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О нет, что делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Костя, дай мне бутылку коньяка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Ту, которая стоит справа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот эту бутылку?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Нет, дай мне другую. Да, эту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф забрал наш коньяк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо забрать эту бутылку назад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я не могу к нему подойти.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай, Костя, ты должен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Костя, это просто ужас!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Kostya, this is just a nightmare!' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'Kostya' straight to 'horror'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня отравился нашим коньяком.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya got poisoned by our cognac.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'Senya' with 'cognac'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "О нет, что делать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh no, what to do?' Kostya links 'about' directly with 'no' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Костя, дай мне бутылку коньяка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Kostya, give me a bottle of cognac.' Chef Viktor combines 'Kostya' with 'cognac' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Ту, которая стоит справа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The one that stands on the right.' Chef Viktor links 'that one' directly with 'who' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот эту бутылку?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This bottle right here?' Kostya combines 'there' with 'a bottle' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Нет, дай мне другую. Да, эту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, give me another one. Yes, this one.' Notice how 'no' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'this'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф забрал наш коньяк!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef took our cognac!' Max links 'chef' directly with 'takes it back' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Надо забрать эту бутылку назад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We need to take this bottle back.' Max links 'it is necessary' directly with 'take' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Я не могу к нему подойти.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I can not approach him.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'I' with 'to walk up to'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Давай, Костя, ты должен.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Come on, Kostya, you must.' Listen for the word meaning 'let's' right alongside 'Kostya' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятно, давай дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
